From 8a56670ee02cf655dc2ad1f8e9a62503e2c39539 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mirko Brombin <9479903+mirkobrombin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 17:26:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] mm: collect delayed ISO16 reuse labels without moving
 pages

Add the MTS M0 observe-mode collector behind CONFIG_MTS_OBSERVE. An
eight-byte page_ext descriptor records the v0.2 metadata word. Hooks in the
classic and multi-generation reclaim paths update age and access evidence
without changing any reclaim or placement decision.

Use a bounded lock-free sample table to label reuse after a configurable
horizon. A pool-adjacent-violators pass calibrates the 16 age buckets.
Debugfs and tracepoints expose sample collisions, labels, and Brier error.
This keeps the hot path allocation-free and predictor quality measurable.

Document both boot parameters. Define sample_shift=0 as sample-all mode to
avoid a zero-width hash operation.

Signed-off-by: Mirko Brombin <9479903+mirkobrombin@users.noreply.github.com>
